  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar Acute Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar faces severe threats to civilian safety due to intense armed conflict, widespread landmine contamination, internal displacement, and extreme weather conditions. The conflict has significantly escalated since October 2023, resulting in a 50% increase in displacement over 6 months.  

Following the Needs and the Gaps this response will address these through the sectors of WASH, MPC and Protection. This programming will be implemented in 5 states namely:  
Southern Shan (Pinlaung and Pekon Township), 
Kayah (Shadaw, Hpruso and Loikaw Township), 
Rakhine (Minbya, Ponnagyun, Kyauktaw and Pauktaw Township) 
Magway (Pakokku township) 
Sagaing (Myinmu, Ayadaw, and Tabayin townships)</narrative>
  </description>
